ngli Zou; Hao Yan; Yan Liu\n\nJ. Phys. Chem. C (2013) 117 (24): 12735–12744. https://doi.org/10.1021/jp312422n\n\n### Band Gap Tuning in ZnO Through Ni Doping via Spray Pyrolysis\n\nSanjoy C. Das; Robert J. Green; Jiban Podder; Tom Z. Regier; Gap Soo Chang; Alexander Moewes\n\nJ. Phys. Chem. C (2013) 117 (24): 12745–12753. https://doi.org/10.1021/jp3126329\n\nAbstract\n\nView Articletitled, Band Gap Tuning in ZnO Through Ni Doping via Spray Pyrolysis\n\nOpen the PDF for Band Gap Tuning in ZnO Through Ni Doping via Spray Pyrolysis in another window\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\"Quantum Efficiency Modification Of Organic Fluorophores Using Gold Nan\" by Suchetan Pal, Palash Dutta et al. (https://stars.library.ucf.edu/scopus2010/7104/)\nciteturn56search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.4 years ago; Crawled: 4 weeks ago; Pal, Suchetan; Dutta, Palash; Wang, Haining; Deng, Zhengtao; and Zou, Shengli, \"Quantum Efficiency Modification Of Organic Fluorophores Using Gold Nanoparticles On Dna Origami Scaffolds\" (2013).\n\n## Scopus Export 2010-2014\n\n \n\n# Quantum Efficiency Modification Of Organic Fluorophores Using Gold Nanoparticles On Dna Origami Scaffolds\n\n  * Suchetan Pal, Arizona State University\n  * Palash Dutta, Arizona State University\n  * Haining Wang, University of Central Florida\n  * Zhengtao Deng, Arizona State University\n  * Shengli Zou, University of Central Florida\n\n## Abstract\n\nWe used DNA origami as a platform to coassemble a 20 nm gold nanoparticle (AuNP) and an organic fluorophore (TAMRA) and studied the distance-dependent plasmonic interactions between the particle and the dye using steady state fluorescence and lifetime measurements. Greater fluorescence quenching was found at smaller dye-particle distances, which was accompanied by an enhancement of the decay rate. We also fabricated 20 and 30 nm AuNP homodimers using DNA origami scaffolds and positioned a Cy3 fluorophore between the AuNPs in both assemblies. For each particle size, three different interparticle distances were investigated. Up to 50% enhancement of the Cy3 fluorescence quantum efficiency was observed for the dye between the 30 nm AuNPs. These results are in good agreement with the theoretical simulations. © 2013 American Chemical Society.\n\n## Publication Date\n\n6-20-2013\n\n## Publication Title\n\nJournal of Physical Chemistry C\n\n## Volume\n\n117\n\n## Issue\n\n24\n\n## Number of Pages\n\n12735-12744\n\n## Document Type\n\nArticle\n\n## Personal Identifier\n\nscopus\n\n## DOI Link\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1021/jp312422n\n\n## Copyright Status\n\nUnknown\n\n## Socpus ID\n\n84879445246 (Scopus)\n\n## STARS Citation\n\nPal, Suchetan; Dutta, Palash; Wang, Haining; Deng, Zhengtao; and Zou, Shengli, \"Quantum Efficiency Modification Of Organic Fluorophores Using Gold Nanoparticles On Dna Origami Scaffolds\" (2013). Scopus Export 2010-2014. 7104.\nhttps://stars.library.ucf.edu/scopus2010/7104\n\nThis document is currently not available here.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQuantum Efficiency Modification of Organic Fluorophores Using Gold Nanoparticles on DNA Origami Scaffolds | The Journal of Physical Chemistry C | ACS Publications (https://pubs.acs.org/doi/abs/10.1021/jp312422n)\nciteturn56search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.4 years ago; Crawled: last month; # Quantum Efficiency Modification of Organic Fluorophores Using Gold Nanoparticles on DNA Origami Scaffolds\n\nSuchetan Pal;\n\nVolume 117, Issue 24\n\nJune 20, 2013\n\nArticle Contents\n\n  * Abstract\n\n  * Supporting Information\n\n[Button: Article Navigation]\n\nArticle| May 29, 2013\n\nAvailable to Purchase\n\n# Quantum Efficiency Modification of Organic Fluorophores Using Gold Nanoparticles on DNA Origami Scaffolds\n\nSuchetan Pal;\n\nClose author information for Suchetan Pal\n\nSuchetan Pal\n\nDepartment of Chemistry and Biochemistry\n\n,\n\nArizona State University\n\n